    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cac17448_d9ab4630",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T19:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "is that what we wanted? a single digest over everything? not a separate digest for each range?\nworks for me, just wondering if there could be reasons to choose the other option.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1cc3759_b3003a8b",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T20:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why would we care about separate hashes for different areas, this is either pass or fail check, right?\n\nHaving a single hash saves a lot or room in the flash.",
      "parentUuid": "cac17448_d9ab4630",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8dbf4871_3630bf4a",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T19:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "iiuc we separate the header from the payload since when the regions are specified we receive only the payload.\ninstead, can we just ask the caller to send both the header+payload (and combine it in a single structure).\n\nyes, it adds some info duplication (total size and num_ranges field), but checks \u0026 handling become simpler. and it\u0027s easier to deal with future changes to the format if we ever need them. one thing we can do right now is to include some versioning field in the header from the beginning. from experience, we will change something at some point, and version will be invaluable for that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af3b8988_92785088",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T20:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would rather avoid duplication with the transfer payload. How about I make the num_ranges field uint16_t and add a uint16_t  version number to this header, but leave the transfer payload as is. \n\nWhen and if we decide to change the payload format we can add a different vendor command.",
      "parentUuid": "8dbf4871_3630bf4a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9325c9c_dd464b5e",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T19:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "uint16_t oruint8_t is probably enough for num_ranges\ncan we add some version field using the rest of the bits instead?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc83cbc1_17006d15",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 53,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T20:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sure, will do,",
      "parentUuid": "b9325c9c_dd464b5e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c74b477b_6b44cd71",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T19:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if we are doing it, can we just do the full-size digest? we are not saving much by truncating it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b2ebc14_e86b711c",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T20:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Frankly, I just don\u0027t see a point, this is a simple integrity check, it is not supposed to be cryptographically strong. I would use crc32, but it is not available in Cr50.",
      "parentUuid": "c74b477b_6b44cd71",
