    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61225c6f_d9aabece",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 189,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T19:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "can we ensure it in a more predictable way (udelay(1000)), not through cflush()? we only need this stabilization delay once, not for every range, right?\nand if we need to ensure a delay, shall it become a part of usb_spi_sha256_start()?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 189,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 189,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e38acb26_788acf85",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 189,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T20:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, moving it to usb_spi_sha256_start() is a good idea. I did not do it because in the other use case (flashrom programming) it is guaranteed to be called well in advance, but the delay belongs there.",
      "parentUuid": "61225c6f_d9aabece",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 189,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 189,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "91ddfaa8_f00bd84e",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 200,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T19:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: something like \"AP RO Verification: FAILED\" for failure and \"AP RO Verification: SUCCESS\" for success.\nEasier for an eye to distinguish, possibly easier for a script to capture as well.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 200,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "acf0fa13_9f8d36dd",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 200,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T20:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll change it, but I was going to two distinctly different messages, thought it would be easier to spot the outcome when messages, but not a bid deal either way.",
      "parentUuid": "91ddfaa8_f00bd84e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 200,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "376d014b_fb391dbe",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 213,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T19:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "maybe cflush() before returning? to have a predictable ordering between console messages and command completion",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 213,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63d37451_075818b9",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 213,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T20:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see a reason: cflush() does not change the order of console messages, it just makes sure that they are not dropped on the floor.",
      "parentUuid": "376d014b_fb391dbe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 213,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c2c604cc_fdf5f242",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 213,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-12T22:59:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "right. I mean when testing the guaranteed ordering between messages printed to the console and sending the response for this command. in theory, we could send the response before the message is flushed to the console, so if some script goes and looks at the console as soon as the command is finished, it may not yet see it there.\nin practice, highly unlikely to have that much of a delay (I guess), so not a big deal.\njust to clarify that I didn\u0027t mean the ordering between different messages, but the ordering between the console messages and command completion.",
      "parentUuid": "63d37451_075818b9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 213,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1112ea7a_f39f23ba",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 213,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-12T23:34:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I see what you mean. In this case the vendor command is sent by the AP, and the console is not really monitored, I don\u0027t think we should delay vendor command response.",
      "parentUuid": "c2c604cc_fdf5f242",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 213,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68406a73_764d251a",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T19:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d suggest for unification purposes to treat this info as S/N. i.e. store in INFO1, require a special image to erase. to avoid using different mechanisms and policies for the data with the same level of importance and same lifetime",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 230,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "336b86ba_05153a69",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-07T20:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, last I heard was that we might have to reprogram the RO and as a result update this value. Also, keeping it separate from INFO1 would make the factory process more flexible, when this value could be erased until the device is finalized (this policy is not yet supported, but I have been thinking about it).\n\nFor these reasons I put it in a separate space.",
      "parentUuid": "68406a73_764d251a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 230,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28e84d3d_d0799b12",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-12T22:59:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "let\u0027s finalize this once we get the decision on \u003crewritable\u003e vs \u003cbetter protection for a one-time-set data\u003e. note that one-time set doesn\u0027t mean set at factory (INFO1 is still writable, just not readable).\nyes, if we want it to be rewritable (we don\u0027t support it atm anyways with this code, though), this is the way to do it.",
      "parentUuid": "336b86ba_05153a69",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 230,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9693dcfd_81aadf6d",
        "filename": "common/ap_ro_integrity_check.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-12T23:34:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sure, who is supposed to decide? I can see an issue where a customer wants to replace the AP RO for whatever reason, even though it has not yet happened.\n\nAn alternative could be keeping multiple instance of the hash database in INFO1, but this is a bit non-deterministic, we don\u0027t know how big this database is, not sure how much room we can have in INFO1 for this purpose, etc.",
      "parentUuid": "28e84d3d_d0799b12",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 230,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "753296edf473300b7825dbcdb11cba7f0afd6aa2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
